{"change_summary":"No additional code changes were required in this Apply Fixes pass. The latest review approved the remaining-depth root-zone oxygenation saturation change and the habitat-geometry probe deduplication update with no blocking follow-up requested.","outstanding_risks":["This stage relied on the latest approved validation results rather than rerunning a fresh workspace-wide test suite.","Two non-blocking cleanup opportunities remain from review: initialization-time `from_parts` still discards the returned `SubstrateOxygenationBreakdown`, and `root_oxygenation_active_biomass_g()` still recomputes the habitat registry internally.","The current `effective_penetration_cm` path no longer has an extra explicit clamp to total depth; review confirmed the math keeps it bounded, but the removed safety-net clamp remains a non-blocking review note."],"steps":[{"description":"Inspect the latest approved review results to confirm whether any blocking amendments were requested for the implemented root-zone oxygenation and habitat-geometry probe fixes.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Apply additional code changes for review follow-up items.","order":2,"status":"skipped"},{"description":"Record the approved validation state from the latest package test, clippy, formatting, and targeted probe runs.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["Latest review outcome was `approved` with no blocking amendments required.","`cargo test -p tank_core` passed across the full `tank_core` package test suite with zero failures.","`cargo clippy -p tank_core -- -D warnings` passed.","`cargo fmt --all --check` was clean in the latest review validation.","`cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_habitat_geometry_probes -- --nocapture` passed with the intended default shape: the summary runner executed and the 5 individual probe entrypoints were ignored by default.","`cargo clippy -p tank_harness -- -D warnings` passed.","Review also reconfirmed passing substrate/root-zone oxygenation coverage, denitrification coverage, and habitat-geometry probe coverage."]}